                            <p class="finalists__text">
                                The Rudkha Collection draws inspiration from the Jamrud Khatulistiwa (Emerald of the Equator) and the philosophy of the Panji Mask, a symbol of serenity, balance, and wisdom. These values are expressed through organic forms, flowing lines, and harmonious proportions rather than a literal interpretation of the mask itself. Crafted from solid teak, natural rattan, and locally sourced materials, the collection brings together Indonesia’s cultural identity and the enduring quality of traditional craftsmanship in a contemporary furniture design.
