                                The SELA Collection is built around the concept of Boundary Overlap, exploring how distinct elements can connect and interact while preserving their individual identities. This idea is combined with the Indonesian philosophy of Bhinneka Tunggal Ika (Unity in Diversity), making the relationship between structure, materials, function, and proportion the foundation of the design process. Crafted from mindi wood, woven water hyacinth and rattan, and bouclé fabric, the collection creates contemporary furniture that balances the unique character of each material within a cohesive design.
